aldria. A transformer tender of about C$900M is due to award in Q1 2027.\n  - Norvane Utilities plans a 12% increase, with a C$450M tender due in Q2 2027.\n  - Both utilities' October filings are mostly for substations and transformers.\n  - This rests on one source, the 2027 utility tender calendar. It shows budgets and tenders, not orders placed.\n- **Data centres (rising, but slower):**\n  - Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026 because power availability limits new sites.\n  - The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months.\n  - The long wait means demand is backed up and will likely be spread over several years.\n  - Connection requests are only a proxy for equipment purchases.\n- **VLTX:** VLTX holdings won 60% of the last tender round. Nobody checked how much of VLTX's orders come from each buyer, so how much it benefits from this is unconfirmed.\n- **Funding:** Whether the utilities can pay for these plans is a separate question. The debt-market answer was that markets are open only for stronger issuers. The equity-market answer was that equity is mostly not a reliable source. Those findings are in n3's work (n5, n6).\n\nThe two sub-answers are in n7.r1 (utilities) and n8.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":3202,"type":"result","duration_ms":64585,"uuid":"549d1716-1971-4017-9a1e-155bac344c94","ttft_stream_ms":1904,"time_to_request_ms":167,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":38,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":6,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":16,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":10,"request_build":19},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_t